 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hey, how's your day been so far?",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 0.79,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_10"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Good, good. Thanks.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.75,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_23"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "The window in my bedroom won't stay open. It just slams down.",
   "est_sec": 3.82,
   "gap_before": 0.29,
   "block": "home_repair.dlg19",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Is it a sash window, the kind that slides up and down?",
   "est_sec": 3.82,
   "gap_before": 1.1,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "home_repair.dlg19"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Yes, an old one. Wooden.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.5,
   "block": "home_repair.dlg19",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Those use cords and weights hidden in the frame. If it slams down, a cord has probably snapped.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 0.36,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "home_repair.dlg19"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Can I fix that, or is it a nightmare?",
   "est_sec": 2.89,
   "gap_before": 3.42,
   "block": "home_repair.dlg19",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "It's fiddly but doable if you're patient. You remove the beading, take out the sash, and tie in a new cord.",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.48,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "home_repair.dlg19"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Honestly,",
   "est_sec": 0.41,
   "gap_before": 0.44,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "home_repair.dlg19"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "that sounds above my pay grade.",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 2.65,
   "block": "home_repair.dlg19",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Fair enough. A window restorer can do it quickly. For now, prop it with a block of wood so it doesn't trap any fingers.",
   "est_sec": 7.54,
   "gap_before": 1.13,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "home_repair.dlg19"
  }
